00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:43.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.434
-We have a great show.

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:48.467
Chris Pratt is here!
Elizabeth Vargas is joining us!

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:50.534
And we have music
from Maisie Peters.

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.534
Let's go write
some Thank You Notes.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:54.367
Come on, now.

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:56.601
[ The Roots rapping ]

00:05:56.601 --> 00:06:03.067
♪♪

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:05.267
-Hey!

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:06.868
Happy Friday, everybody.
Today is Friday.

00:06:06.868 --> 00:06:08.934
And that's usually when I catch
up on some personal stuff.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:11.767
I check my inbox, I return
some e-mails, of course,

00:06:11.767 --> 00:06:13.901
and I write out some
Thank You Notes on Fridays.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:16.033
Yeah, I do it every --

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:17.834
I was just --
I was just wondering.

00:06:17.834 --> 00:06:19.300
I'm running a bit behind today.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.901
I thought, if you guys
wouldn't mind, I'd like to write

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:24.033
out my weekly Thank You Notes
right now during the show.

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:25.467
Is that okay?

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:27.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.801
Thank you. Thank you.
Thank you very much.

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:31.434
James, can I get some Thank
You Note writing music, please?

00:06:31.434 --> 00:06:32.767
♪♪

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:34.100
Alright.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.100
Oh, he's good.
-Chewing gum? What?

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.434
-Yeah. I don't know.

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:43.534
♪♪

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:45.033
Thank you,
Major League Baseball's

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:46.968
new 15-second pitch clock.

00:06:46.968 --> 00:06:49.000
15 seconds
might not seem that long,

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.834
or, as Stormy Daniels put it,
"I beg to differ."

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:54.000
-Whey! Ohh!

00:06:57.834 --> 00:06:59.934
Indicated. Lick it.

00:06:59.934 --> 00:07:02.400
-No.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.701
♪♪

00:07:03.701 --> 00:07:08.033
Thank you, Florida Atlantic's
mascot Owlsley,

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:11.767
for looking like
the world's angriest Cinnabon.

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:12.934
Mad.

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:15.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.133
-Err!
-He's mad, but delicious.

00:07:17.133 --> 00:07:20.434
-He's mad but delicious!
Get a six-pack.

00:07:20.434 --> 00:07:23.901
-Thank you, the people who keep
their ID and credit cards

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:26.100
in their phone case,
for saying to the world,

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:29.601
"Eh, if I lose something,
it might as well be everything."

00:07:29.601 --> 00:07:31.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.801 --> 00:07:34.100
"Just take it all.
Just take it all!"

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.968
-"Just take it all."

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:38.901
-Well, can you call your wife?
-No. I can't even -- No.

00:07:38.901 --> 00:07:40.234
Legally married anymore.

00:07:40.234 --> 00:07:43.367
My wedding certificate's
in it, too.

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:45.100
-The deed to my house.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.467 --> 00:07:47.801
♪♪

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:49.467
-Thank you, glass,

00:07:49.467 --> 00:07:52.767
for being the one thing
that's worth more stained.

00:07:52.767 --> 00:07:55.801
-Ohh. Nice.
That's a thinker.

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:58.067
Yeah, that's a thinker.

00:07:58.067 --> 00:07:59.968
-That's one of those --
You snap to that one.

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:01.801
-That's a snapper.
-Yeah. You don't clap.

00:08:01.801 --> 00:08:03.300
You think about it,
and you go...

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.634
-"Yeah, Daddy-o. I grock."

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:07.067
-Let me do it again.
I'll finish it up again.

00:08:07.067 --> 00:08:08.267
Try it again. Ready?
[ Clears throat ]

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:11.467
-Everybody snap.

00:08:11.467 --> 00:08:13.200
-Thank you, glass,

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.334
for being the one thing
that's worth more stained.

00:08:16.334 --> 00:08:18.167
[ Fingers snapping ]

00:08:18.167 --> 00:08:20.901
[ Jazz music plays ]

00:08:20.901 --> 00:08:22.534
-I can dig it.

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:23.968
♪♪

00:08:23.968 --> 00:08:25.767
Yeah, man.

00:08:25.767 --> 00:08:28.501
He's a cool cat.
-Yeah.

00:08:28.501 --> 00:08:30.334
-He's got his pen.

00:08:30.334 --> 00:08:32.767
[ Music stops ]

00:08:32.767 --> 00:08:35.100
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.467
♪♪

00:08:39.467 --> 00:08:42.467
-Thank you, Cinderella,
for being the beautiful story

00:08:42.467 --> 00:08:44.767
of a woman
who catfishes a prince.

00:08:44.767 --> 00:08:47.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.133 --> 00:08:50.801
[ Applause ]

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:52.133
-"My shoe."

00:08:54.234 --> 00:08:55.701
♪♪

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:58.868
-Thank you, third time guessing
a computer password,

00:08:58.868 --> 00:09:01.200
for letting me know
the feeling of what it's like

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.868
to defuse a bomb.

00:09:02.868 --> 00:09:04.567
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.567 --> 00:09:08.000
"Yes! We're in!

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.701
Cut the blue wire!"

00:09:13.667 --> 00:09:14.934
♪♪

00:09:14.934 --> 00:09:17.601
Thank you, sinks with
hot and cold faucets,

00:09:17.601 --> 00:09:20.033
for making me feel like
a water deejay.

00:09:20.033 --> 00:09:22.801
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my Thank You Notes.

